{"id":"beats-3210ed","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add a `beats link` command to add a dependency between two issues; support the -t --type options to specify the kind of dependency","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:57.566632Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-3210ed","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-02-10T14:24:21.912872Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-3210ed","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a4b1f100-39db-4a23-8797-b156feb2f956","text":"Walkthrough:\n\n- Added beats link command (cmd/beats/link.go) to enable linking issues with dependency types via CLI.\n- Command syntax: beats link \u003csource-id\u003e \u003ctarget-id\u003e -t \u003ctype\u003e\n- Supported types: blocks, blocked_by, depends_on, dependency_of, duplicates, duplicated_by, relates_to.\n- Issues and types validated. Error output for invalid args.\n- Links are appended as UPDATE events to .beats/issues.db, visible via show.\n- Multiple link types allowed, error handling for invalid types tested.\n- Tested with live issues: confirm dependencies are shown in history and Dependencies block.\n- Edge cases, error scenarios, and reciprocal links are handled cleanly."},"created_at":"2026-02-10T15:12:02.590259Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-3210ed","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-02-10T15:12:06.805462Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-dece42","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Standardize status icons and redesign backlog view","description":"Create SVG circle-based StatusIcon component and redesign backlog view with 4 collapsible status-grouped tables inspired by Linear.","labels":["UI"]},"created_at":"2026-02-10T15:33:46.52826Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-dece42","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-02-10T15:34:05.178737Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-dece42","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-40cf5137-2854-48d3-82ce-37f5106a1e58","text":"Walkthrough: Added shared StatusIcon component with SVG icons for all statuses (BACKLOG=dashed circle, PLANNED=outlined circle, DOING=half-filled, BLOCKED=filled with X, DONE=filled with checkmark). Redesigned Backlog view with collapsible sections, table layout, and refined label badges. Replaced all emoji indicators with StatusIcon in Board and Dashboard views. Verified visually across all views."},"created_at":"2026-02-10T16:42:57.248861Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-dece42","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-02-10T16:43:02.325069Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-ace6f6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Linear-style UI redesign","description":"Redesign the beats web application to match Linear's look and feel: left sidebar navigation, ultra-dark flat monochrome palette, compact typography, and clean minimalist interactions.","labels":["epic"]},"created_at":"2026-05-18T06:36:26.19901Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-ace6f6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-18T06:36:43.516307Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-ace6f6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-17a75a14-e49f-415c-bc37-fb96ddfd96dd","text":"Completed Linear-style UI redesign across all 8 phases:\n\nPhase 1: New design system with Linear-aligned dark theme tokens (ultra-dark backgrounds, muted borders, monochrome text palette, status/label colors)\nPhase 2: Converted layout from top navigation to 240px left sidebar with vertical nav items\nPhase 3: Overhauled all UI primitives (Button, Card, Badge, Modal, Progress) - removed glass/glow effects, flat styling\nPhase 4: Rewrote Backlog as Linear-style issue list with tab bar (All Issues/Active/Backlog), collapsible status groups, compact 36px rows\nPhase 5: Updated Board view with flat column headers, clean issue cards\nPhase 6: Replaced modal-based issue detail with full-width slide-over panel with breadcrumb, properties sidebar, popover menus\nPhase 7: Updated Dashboard (compact metrics), Dependencies (flat rows), PendingEventsPanel (simplified)\nPhase 8: Cleaned up stale CSS references, verified TypeScript compilation and Vite build\n\nNew files: design_docs/DESIGN.md, web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx\nModified: 15 source files across index.css, Layout, Backlog, Board, Dashboard, Dependencies, IssueDetailModal, PendingEventsPanel, App, and all UI primitives"},"created_at":"2026-05-18T07:29:26.548521Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-ace6f6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7179ca56-3bbb-43ad-98ed-25a341e9a7be","text":"Second pass - UX quality improvements:\n\n1. Issue detail converted from slide-over to full inline page (replaces main content, sidebar stays). Breadcrumb navigation with pagination arrows (10/10) and keyboard nav (j/k/arrows).\n2. Empty status groups now collapse by default instead of showing 'No issues' padding that wasted 80% of viewport.\n3. Sidebar restructured with section grouping: primary nav (Issues, Board) separated from secondary (Dashboard, Dependencies) with 'INSIGHTS' label. Sidebar narrowed to 220px.\n4. Board Done column capped at 5 cards with '+ N more' expand, preventing wall-of-cards. Cards use title-first layout with shortened hash IDs.\n5. Issue row title now has font-medium weight for visual hierarchy. Rows tightened to 38px.\n6. Fixed Makefile build order: frontend must build BEFORE Go binary since static files are go:embed'd."},"created_at":"2026-05-18T08:15:56.661477Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-477ca3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Command palette (Cmd+K)","description":"Implement a Linear-style command palette accessible via Cmd+K (or Ctrl+K).\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Fuzzy search across all issues by title, ID, and labels\n- Quick actions: change status, assign labels, set estimate on current/selected issue\n- Navigation: jump to any view (Issues, Board, Dashboard, Dependencies)\n- Create new issue inline from the palette\n- Recent items / frequently accessed shortcuts\n\n## Design\n\n- Centered modal overlay with search input at top\n- Results grouped by type (Issues, Actions, Navigation)\n- Keyboard navigation (arrow keys to select, Enter to execute, Esc to close)\n- Each result row shows icon + title + metadata","labels":["epic"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.711693Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-274e84","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Global keyboard shortcuts","description":"Add keyboard shortcuts throughout the application for power-user efficiency.\n\n## Shortcuts\n\n- `C` — Create new issue (open modal)\n- `/` or `Cmd+K` — Focus search / open command palette\n- `S` — Change status (when viewing an issue)\n- `L` — Change labels (when viewing an issue)\n- `E` — Change estimate (when viewing an issue)\n- `Esc` — Go back / close current view\n- `1-5` — Quick-set status (Backlog/Planned/Doing/Blocked/Done) when an issue is focused\n\n## Notes\n\n- Shortcuts should be disabled when an input/textarea is focused\n- Show shortcut hints in tooltips and the command palette","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.73854Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-e1ee26","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Board drag-and-drop","description":"Enable drag-and-drop on the kanban board to change issue status by moving cards between columns.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Drag a card from one column to another to update its status\n- Visual feedback during drag (ghost card, drop target highlight)\n- Optimistic UI update with draft event created on drop\n- Consider using a lightweight DnD library (e.g. `@dnd-kit/core`) or native HTML drag API\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Dragging to the same column should be a no-op\n- Handle rapid successive drags gracefully","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.764412Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8e74b1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Inline issue creation from backlog","description":"Add quick inline issue creation directly from the backlog status group headers.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Clicking the `+` button on a status group header (or pressing `C` while focused) inserts an editable row at the top of that group\n- User types a title and presses Enter to create\n- Escape cancels\n- New issue gets the status of the group it was created in\n- After creation, the row resets for another quick entry\n\n## Design\n\n- The inline row should match the visual style of regular issue rows\n- Auto-focus the title input immediately\n- Show a subtle placeholder like 'New issue...'","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.793423Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-533f00","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Sub-issue hierarchy and epic grouping","description":"Surface the parent-child relationship in the UI so epics can contain and organize sub-issues.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- In the backlog: show sub-issues nested under their parent with indent and collapse/expand\n- In issue detail: show a 'Sub-issues' section listing children with status icons and progress\n- In issue detail: show 'Parent' breadcrumb link if the issue has a `parent_id`\n- On epics: show completion progress (e.g., 3/5 sub-issues done)\n\n## Data Model\n\n- Already supported via `parent_id` field on issues\n- No backend changes needed, purely frontend rendering\n\n## Design\n\n- Indented rows in backlog with a subtle tree line\n- Collapsible sub-issue groups\n- Progress bar on epic rows showing sub-issue completion","labels":["epic"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.820953Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a3e1c7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Sort and filter controls","description":"Add sort and filter UI to the backlog tab bar.\n\n## Filter By\n\n- Label (multi-select)\n- Status (multi-select, in addition to tab-based filtering)\n- Assignee\n- Has estimate / no estimate\n\n## Sort By\n\n- Created date (default)\n- Updated date\n- Estimate (high to low)\n- Title (alphabetical)\n\n## Design\n\n- Filter icon button in the tab bar opens a dropdown with filter options\n- Active filters shown as removable chips\n- Sort dropdown next to the filter button\n- Persist sort/filter preferences in localStorage","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.84818Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-5894eb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"URL routing for deep linking","description":"Add hash-based routing so issue views and detail pages are bookmarkable and shareable.\n\n## Routes\n\n- `#/issues` — Backlog/issues list\n- `#/issues/:id` — Issue detail page\n- `#/board` — Board view\n- `#/dashboard` — Dashboard view\n- `#/dependencies` — Dependencies view\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Browser back/forward navigation works correctly\n- Opening a direct link to an issue loads the detail page\n- View state (active tab, selected issue) syncs with URL\n- Use `hashchange` event listener, no router library needed\n\n## Notes\n\n- Keep it lightweight — no react-router dependency\n- Hash-based routing works with the Go embedded static file server without any server-side routing changes","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:03:16.873494Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-274e84","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-274e84","target_id":"beats-477ca3","kind":"relates_to"}]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:04:11.809498Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8e74b1","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-8e74b1","target_id":"beats-477ca3","kind":"relates_to"}]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:04:11.837921Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a49ec2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dependencies: blocking chain visualization","description":"Replace the flat relationship list with a directed graph/tree view that shows blocking chains.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Visualize `blocks` / `blocked_by` relationships as a tree or DAG\n- Show the critical path: which issues need to unblock first\n- Color-code nodes by status (done blockers = resolved, doing = in progress)\n- Collapsed by default, expand to see full chains\n- Highlight circular dependencies as warnings\n\n## Design\n\n- Tree layout: root nodes are issues that block others, leaves are the blocked issues\n- Each node shows: status icon, title (truncated), ID\n- Clicking a node navigates to the issue detail\n- Resolved blockers shown with muted/strikethrough styling","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:19:38.452302Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8d6b52","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dependencies: status-aware relationship display","description":"Show inline status context on dependency rows so users can see at a glance whether blockers are resolved.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Each relationship row shows both issues with their current status icons\n- If a `blocked_by` target is DONE, show a 'resolved' indicator (e.g., green checkmark, muted styling)\n- If a `blocked_by` target is still in progress, show it prominently\n- Add a summary line at the top: 'N of M blockers resolved'\n\n## Notes\n\n- This is a refinement of the existing dependency rows, not a full rewrite","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:19:38.486169Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a79a91","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dashboard: velocity and burndown chart","description":"Add a velocity or burndown chart showing issue completion over time.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Line or bar chart showing issues completed per week (or per day for recent data)\n- Data source: `created_at` and status change timestamps from the event log\n- Show trend: is the team accelerating or slowing down?\n- Simple SVG-based chart, no charting library needed\n\n## Design\n\n- Card in the dashboard below the metrics row\n- X-axis: time periods (weeks), Y-axis: issue count\n- Two series: created vs completed\n- Muted grid lines, colored lines for the data","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:19:38.513314Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-ab8ef1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dashboard: stale issue detection","description":"Highlight issues that may need attention because they've been stagnant.\n\n## Rules\n\n- **Stale in-progress**: issues with status DOING that haven't been updated in \u003e 7 days\n- **Aging backlog**: issues with status BACKLOG that were created \u003e 30 days ago with no activity\n- **Blocked too long**: issues with status BLOCKED for \u003e 3 days\n\n## Design\n\n- A 'Needs Attention' section in the dashboard\n- Each stale issue shown as a compact row with: status icon, title, time since last update, reason tag ('stale', 'aging', 'blocked')\n- Clicking navigates to the issue detail","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:19:38.540602Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-49c21a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dashboard: label distribution breakdown","description":"Show a breakdown of issues by label to understand the composition of the backlog.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Horizontal bar chart or segmented bar showing issue count per label\n- Filter: show all issues, or only active (non-DONE) issues\n- Each bar colored with the label's color token\n- Show count and percentage\n\n## Design\n\n- Card in the dashboard\n- Simple horizontal bars, label name on left, count on right\n- Sorted by count descending","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:19:38.568141Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8faf44","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dashboard: recent activity feed","description":"Add a project-level activity timeline showing the latest changes across all issues.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Show the last 20-30 events across all issues\n- Event types: issue created, status changed, comment added, labels changed, estimate changed\n- Each entry: avatar, author name, action description, issue title (linked), relative time\n- System events as one-liners (like in issue detail), comments with preview text\n\n## Data Source\n\n- Read from the events in `issues.db` (already available via the storage layer)\n- May need a new API endpoint: `GET /api/activity` returning recent events with payloads\n\n## Design\n\n- Full-width section in the dashboard, below the metrics\n- Matches the activity timeline styling from the issue detail view","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:19:38.594972Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-ace6f6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-41abe6bb-2968-4c2e-8739-58a467d1905f","text":"## Final Summary\n\nCompleted a full Linear-style UI redesign of the beats web application across multiple sessions.\n\n### Major Changes\n\n- **Layout**: Converted from top navigation to left sidebar with section grouping (Issues/Board + Insights)\n- **Theme**: Ultra-dark flat palette matching Linear's exact colors (rgb 22,23,24 cards, rgb 228,228,231 text)\n- **Issue List**: Tab bar (All/Active/Backlog), collapsible status groups, compact rows with label badges, search filtering\n- **Issue Detail**: Full inline page (not modal/slide-over) with breadcrumb, pagination, properties sidebar with popover menus for status/estimate/labels\n- **Activity Timeline**: Linear-style layout — system events as one-liners, comments in subtle background cards, markdown rendering via `react-markdown` + `remark-breaks`, Gravatar avatars\n- **Board**: Full-width columns, Done column capped at 5 with expand, title-first card layout\n- **New Issue**: Modal with inline dropdowns (label/status/estimate), portal-based menus\n- **Pending Changes**: Clickable indicator opens delta view showing all pending events with payloads; save respects `auto_commit` config\n- **Infrastructure**: Fixed Makefile build order, added CREATE support to draft API, config endpoint, git user resolution from `git config`, discard endpoint fix\n\n### Files Changed\n\n~20 frontend files (components, CSS, API client) + 3 Go backend files (handlers, router, Makefile)"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:21:23.842532Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
